I'd go along with earlier comments about the doors.  There are just too many
locked doors.  I'd like to suggest what (I think) would be an improvement.  
Locked doors and closed doors should show up as '+'.  Open doors might be
'=' and doorways without doors (or broken locked doors) as '#' or '='.
It is really anoying not to be able to tell the difference between closed and
open doors.  Also when a shopkeeper has a locked door I think a 'keep out',
'do not disturb' or 'private' sign is in order as low level characters get
killed off rather often by this.

